  message: "SATISFIED ON THE FILED INSTANCE; THE GENERAL CLAIM IS NOT ASSERTED. Premise check 2026-09-28 on dev 51c73cce78.\n\nFILED INSTANCE (kotlin, `class A { fun f(): Int = 1 }` / `class B { fun g(): Int = 2 }`): the symbols are still wrong (one top-level function f; no A, B or g) -- the grammar collapse this item describes is unchanged -- but the run now records it: limits.failed_files has {analyzer: kotlin, path: one.kt, reason: \"partial_parse: 1 damaged node(s); analysed from tree-sitter's error recovery, so declarations in or after the damaged region may be missing\"}. The statement allows \"recovers faithfully OR records the degradation (failed_files entry, ...)\", so the instance now meets it. Fixed by WI-bulaz (8a2eb1a0cf, 2026-09-26): record_partial_parse in analyze/base.py, wired into the shared TreeSitterAnalyzer loop and the go, java, js_ts, kotlin, c, objc, csharp, php, ruby and lua loops.\n\nSTALE PARTS OF THIS ITEM: \"nothing controls this one\" (WI-bulaz ships a production-path test, test_partial_parse_disclosure.py); \"real-corpus frequency unmeasured\" (WI-bulaz measured it: crun 74 files, AFNetworking 34, phoenix 114, hummingbird 7, alertmanager 0). The \"has_error alone is not the signal\" caution is answered as a disclosure, never a gate -- a correctly recovered file is also listed, which over-discloses but never silences. No per-symbol provenance marker exists; the disclosure is per file.\n\nRESIDUAL, ALREADY FILED: WI-tikul -- 24 analyzers with their own analyze() loop are not wired (re-enumerated today: matlab latex racket r_lang meson robot svelte rst thrift purescript vue starlark proto scheme puppet scss cmake css dockerfile json_config yaml_ansible make toml_config xml_config). Positive evidence it still bites: starlark, `def f(x:` (broken) then `def g()` -> only the file node, both f and g lost, failed_files empty; the clean control emits f and g. The starlark repro is added to WI-tikul."  # e822
